  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Ship to Shore Rights South East Asia: Regional Programme on Labour Migration in the Fishing Sector</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The programme is jointly implemented by ILO, IOM and UNDP and aims to promote regular and safe labour migration among South East Asian countries, in particular in the fishing and seafood processing industry. IOM&apos;s interventions under the programme will focus on conducting supply chain assessments for the fishing sector, supporting counterparts with implementing standardized victim of trafficking identification and referral at the national and bilateral levels, building national capacities on integrated return and reintegration support to victims of trafficking and vulnerable migrants, and outreach and awareness raising on safe migration.</narrative>
  </description>
